A||||9||Cooter||A child's letter to Santa||||1||
Z||000000||Cooter||12-18-2001||10:17 PM||||One of my assignments today was to have the kids (second grade) write a letter to Santa. Even the kids who don't believe in him wrote good letters. Many did not even ask for anything- they wanted to know how Mrs. Claus was and wondered about the reindeer. But this letter really got my attention:<P>Dear Santa,<P>When you come to my house, you had better leave all the toys for me. If you don't I will punch you in the eye and kick your bottom back up into the sky.<P>Love,<BR>*********<P>Guess who gets a lump of coal in their stocking?||||reg||1
